.superpowers/

# Generated datasets: the full two-year set is ~250 MB, regenerate with
#   go run ./cmd/lapdog-gen -dir .dataset
.dataset/
.dataset.db
.dataset.db-wal
.dataset.db-shm

# Build output. Rebuild with `make build-ctl`, `make build-gen`, `make build-windows`.
# Note: not "*.lpd" — the committed capture fixtures under testdata/fixtures must
# stay tracked, since tests and reviewers depend on them.
#
# Anchored to the repository root. An unanchored "dist/" matches a directory of
# that name at any depth, which also caught internal/web/dist — so the frontend
# bundle that is meant to be committed was ignored, except for index.html, which
# had been added before the rule existed. That left the worst possible state: a
# clone contained HTML referencing hashed assets that were not in the repository,
# so the binary built and started but served a blank page.
/dist/
